Have any governments or intelligence agencies
ever accessed private user messages in the past?

00:47:33.833 --> 00:47:38.333
agencies ever accessed private
user messages in the past?

00:47:38.366 --> 00:47:42.066
- No, never. Telegram has never shared
a single private message with anyone,

00:47:42.133 --> 00:47:45.733
a single private message with anyone, including
governments and intelligence services.

00:47:46.233 --> 00:47:53.066
including governments and intelligence services. If
you try to access any server in any of the data center

00:47:53.100 --> 00:47:58.433
data center locations, it's all encrypted.
You can extract all the hard drives

00:47:59.433 --> 00:48:03.200
and analyze it, but you won't get anything. It's
all encrypted in a way that is undecipherable.

00:48:04.133 --> 00:48:07.166
It's all encrypted in the
way that is undecipherable.

00:48:08.833 --> 00:48:13.933
That was very important for us.
That's why we can say with confidence

00:48:14.833 --> 00:48:23.600
there hasn't been ever a leakage of
data, any leak of data from Telegram.

00:48:23.600 --> 00:48:28.400
Not in terms of private messages,
not in terms of, say, contact lists.

00:48:28.500 --> 00:48:34.933
- Do you see in the future a possible scenario
