04:09:11.700 --> 04:09:15.200
- On the topic of abundance,
offline, we had a lot of

04:09:15.200 --> 04:09:18.833
fascinating philosophical discussions,
one of which was about the mouse

04:09:18.966 --> 04:09:25.666
paradise experiment, also known as
Universe 25. It's an experiment from

04:09:26.300 --> 04:09:33.566
the 1960s and early 70s, conducted
by ethologist John B. Calhoun.

04:09:33.633 --> 04:09:36.933
And we can talk about this
one for hours also, I'm

04:09:37.000 --> 04:09:43.700
sure. But it was an experiment with a few
hundreds of individual mice compartments,

04:09:44.733 --> 04:09:48.600
and they provided them with
unlimited food, water, nesting,

04:09:48.666 --> 04:09:51.766
no predators, stable temperatures,
and frequent cleaning.

04:09:51.800 --> 04:09:55.200
Basically, the definition
of abundance as far as mice

04:09:55.300 --> 04:09:58.933
go. And the interesting
aspect of this experiment

04:09:59.166 --> 04:10:02.600
is that at first the population
doubled, it grew very

04:10:02.666 --> 04:10:10.200
quickly, but then it leveled off, and certain
really negative social things started

04:10:10.366 --> 04:10:14.266
happening. Like mothers neglected or
killed their young. Violent attacks and

04:10:14.300 --> 04:10:16.233
hypersexual activity became widespread.

04:10:17.100 --> 04:10:20.866
Some "beautiful" ones, largely
inactive, well-groomed mice

04:10:20.966 --> 04:10:24.400
withdrew, refusing to mate or
interact. So, all of these kind of

04:10:24.466 --> 04:10:27.966
societal qualities that we see as
negative for the functioning of a

04:10:28.000 --> 04:10:33.966
society started to emerge because
of the abundance, and finally the

04:10:34.033 --> 04:10:37.700
collapse. The reproduction
rates crashed. Social

04:10:37.733 --> 04:10:41.400
dysfunction spread to the next
generation and eventually just went

04:10:41.466 --> 04:10:45.333
extinct. It didn't just
plummet to a low level,

04:10:45.366 --> 04:10:49.333
it plummeted steadily to zero
despite the fact that there

04:10:49.400 --> 04:10:52.300
was ongoing resource abundance. As

04:10:52.400 --> 04:10:58.833
the description states, "The last mice
died surrounded by untouched food and

04:10:59.000 --> 04:11:02.900
water." So, I mean, there's
deep wisdom to that

04:11:02.966 --> 04:11:06.366
about abundance. It seems...
You've mentioned this in different

04:11:06.400 --> 04:11:10.066
contexts throughout this
conversation, is it seems

04:11:10.133 --> 04:11:16.833
like scarcity, it seems like
constraints, it seems like non-abundance

04:11:18.066 --> 04:11:22.200
is essential for human flourishing,
which is a counterintuitive notion.

04:11:23.166 --> 04:11:26.100
It's true for mice, and I think
it's probably true for humans too.

04:11:27.266 --> 04:11:33.200
- We have evolved to overcome
scarcity. Almost by definition there

04:11:33.200 --> 04:11:37.800
has never been such thing
as infinite amount of food

04:11:38.966 --> 04:11:49.200
or entertainment in our lives before now.
We seem as a species to lose our ability

04:11:50.566 --> 04:11:57.800
to identify purpose in a world where you
have everything, and everything loses its

04:11:57.866 --> 04:12:04.733
meaning. Restrictions are important.
I think, though, that they should be

04:12:04.800 --> 04:12:09.366
coming from within. It should be
self-restriction rather than restriction

04:12:10.633 --> 04:12:16.500
in order to create purpose and meaning
in life. In a way, I was lucky in a very

04:12:17.833 --> 04:12:21.233
counterintuitive way because I grew up

04:12:21.266 --> 04:12:28.566
poor. I didn't have money when I was a
teenager. I had the same jacket for years,

04:12:30.500 --> 04:12:36.900
which was bought on a second-hand
marketplace. My father wouldn't receive

04:12:38.066 --> 04:12:41.866
his salary as a university
professor for months because

04:12:43.200 --> 04:12:49.066
the Russian state was almost
bankrupt back then. My mom had to

04:12:50.600 --> 04:12:54.800
juggle two jobs to take care of us. It was

04:12:55.800 --> 04:13:02.266
not easy, but it also created purpose,
it created meaning, it created

04:13:02.366 --> 04:13:09.266
priorities. It allowed us to focus
on things that mattered, allowed us

04:13:09.366 --> 04:13:20.866
to develop our character and intellectual
abilities. Now, if we had everything...

04:13:22.133 --> 04:13:26.266
why do anything? These mice...

04:13:30.666 --> 04:13:36.133
suffered societal collapse that
was irreversible. And this

04:13:37.400 --> 04:13:44.666
is not an accident. This kind of experiment
has been repeated countless times. At a

04:13:44.700 --> 04:13:52.233
certain point, social dysfunction and
the erosion of social roles becomes

04:13:52.300 --> 04:13:59.333
contagious, and the society
gradually degrades into a

04:13:59.400 --> 04:14:03.466
chaotic collection of individuals

04:14:04.500 --> 04:14:09.866
unable to take care of the next generation
or even to produce the next generation,

04:14:11.800 --> 04:14:13.966
and it goes extinct.

04:14:14.000 --> 04:14:17.300
- It's fascinating because we're creating
technologies, and this is what AI

04:14:17.400 --> 04:14:23.600
is proposing to our future generations
as a problem to solve, which

04:14:23.666 --> 04:14:27.600
is AI may very well
create abundance. And so

04:14:27.633 --> 04:14:31.566
we will be like these mice
potentially, whether it's AI or

04:14:31.666 --> 04:14:35.033
other kinds of technologies
that increase and give more and

04:14:35.066 --> 04:14:38.966
more to all of us, and it is a thing
that will decrease the amount of

04:14:39.000 --> 04:14:42.666
suffering in the world, increase the quality
of life. But as we reach towards that

04:14:42.733 --> 04:14:45.900
abundance, the fabric that connects us,

04:14:46.866 --> 04:14:49.666
rooted in our biology that's
developed by evolution

04:14:50.966 --> 04:14:53.266
might create a real challenge for us.

04:14:54.233 --> 04:14:57.000
- We should find the right balance
between chaos and order,

04:14:58.133 --> 04:15:02.033
between self-restriction
and freedom for creativity.

04:15:03.200 --> 04:15:06.833
- Your father recently celebrated
